{"id": "q0091", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 230375063, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "1bd884090589f25ac8e99f9bb754f4b90b4c7a09d6887616d0aefbdba25a74d4", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 7, "query": "Aaron and Vanessa were relay race partners on a running team. Aaron was able to run each mile twice as fast as Vanessa, but Vanessa was able to run twice as far as Aaron did. If Vanessa ran 4 miles and Aaron completed his part of the race in 16 minutes, how long in minutes did Vanessa take to complete her part?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0091.wav", "input_sha256": "c9d30e32f0e214f9a7dea809ed5fa76c96786c710fb1e04c79f4c5680a2736cc", "input_samples": 372000, "input_s": 23.25, "n_real_chunks": 24, "score": 0.2594, "act": 0.9991, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Vanessa ran 4 miles. Since she ran twice as far as Aaron, he ran 2 miles. A aron ran each mile twice as fast as Vanessa, so his time per mile is half of hers. He completed 2 miles in 16 minutes, which means each mile took him 8 minutes. So Va nessa's time per mile would be double that, or 16 minutes per mile. For 4 miles, that' s 4 times 16, which equals 6 4 minutes. 6 4.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 23, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 24, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0091_conservative_local.wav", "sha256": "adc7ff1f43b6edabb9b174c97ab3ca3000e3dcaf8baa74d47ceba43811e3786c"