{"id": "q0184", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1695060334, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "1bd884090589f25ac8e99f9bb754f4b90b4c7a09d6887616d0aefbdba25a74d4", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 7, "query": "A circular opening of radius 0.8mm in an opaque screen is illuminated by plane waves of monochromatic light and the emergent light allowed to fall on a movable screen. As the screen is gradually brought toward the aperture, it is found that a succession of alternately light and dark spots appear at the center of the diffraction patterns. (a) If a bright spot appears for the second time when the distance from the screen to the position of the screen required for a bright spot to appear for the first time is 36.2 cm, find the wavelength of the light. (b) If a dark spot appears for the second time when the distance between the screen and the position of the screen required for a dark spot to appear for the first time is 36.2 cm, find the wavelength of the light. (c) Find at what distance from the screen to the aperture a bright spot appeared for the first time (refer to part (a)). (d) Find at what distance from the screen to the aperture a dark spot appeared for the first time (refer to part (b)).\n\nA. Wavelength of light for bright spot: 1.25 × 10^-6 m, Wavelength of light for dark spot: 460mμ, First bright spot: 57 cm, First dark spot: 69 cm\nB. Wavelength of light for bright spot: 1.17 × 10^-6 m, Wavelength of light for dark spot: 442mμ, First bright spot: 54.7 cm, First dark spot: 72.4 cm\nC. Wavelength of light for bright spot: 1.5 × 10^-6 m, Wavelength of light for dark spot: 500mμ, First bright spot: 55 cm, First dark spot: 72 cm\nD. Wavelength of light for bright spot: 1.3 × 10^-6 m, Wavelength of light for dark spot: 450mμ, First bright spot: 56 cm, First dark spot: 70 cm\nE. Wavelength of light for bright spot: 1.4 × 10^-6 m, Wavelength of light for dark spot: 480mμ, First bright spot: 58 cm, First dark spot: 74 cm\nF. Wavelength of light for bright spot: 1.0 × 10^-6 m, Wavelength of light for dark spot: 420mμ, First bright spot: 52 cm, First dark spot: 75 cm\nG. Wavelength of light for bright spot: 1.3 × 10^-6 m, Wavelength of light for dark spot: 465mμ, First bright spot: 56.5 cm, First dark spot: 70.5 cm\nH. Wavelength of light for bright spot: 1.2 × 10^-6 m, Wavelength of light for dark spot: 440mμ, First bright spot: 54 cm, First dark spot: 73 cm\nI. Wavelength of light for bright spot: 1.1 × 10^-6 m, Wavelength of light for dark spot: 435mμ, First bright spot: 53 cm, First dark spot: 71 cm\nJ. Wavelength of light for bright spot: 1.15 × 10^-6 m, Wavelength of light for dark spot: 450mμ, First bright spot: 55.5 cm, First dark spot: 71.5 cm\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0184.wav", "input_sha256": "15e49d4956f4502392d4e2d29350ef7e9e4a2bfe9d47598ab8080f0e14f26247", "input_samples": 2833000, "input_s": 177.062, "n_real_chunks": 178, "score": 0.9282, "act": 0.9913, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "B. Wavelength of light for bright spot: 1.17 × 10⁻⁶ m. Wavelength of light for dark spot: about 0.442 μm (option B appears to have a unit typo). First bright spot: 54.7 cm. First dark spot: 72.4 cm.", "expert_answer": "**B.** Wavelength of light for bright spot: **1.17 × 10⁻⁶ m**. Wavelength of light for dark spot: **about 0.442 μm** *(option B appears to have a unit typo)*. First bright spot: **54.7 cm**. First dark spot: **72.4 cm**.", "transcript": "A circular opening of radius 0.8 millimeters in an opaque screen is illuminated by plane waves of monochromatic light and the emergent light allowed to fall on a movable screen. As the screen is gradually brought toward the apert