{"id": "q0240", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3432424482, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "1bd884090589f25ac8e99f9bb754f4b90b4c7a09d6887616d0aefbdba25a74d4", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 7, "query": "The economy is currently operating at full employment. Assuming flexible wages and prices how would a decline in aggregate demand affect GDP and the price level in the short run and GDP and the price level in the long run? SHORT-RUN GDP     SHORT-RUN PRICE LEVEL     LONG-RUN GDP     LONG-RUN PRICE LEVEL\n\nA. Falls     No change     No change     Falls\nB. No change     Falls     No change     No change\nC. Falls     Falls     No change     Falls\nD. No change     No change     Falls     Falls\nE. Falls     Falls     Falls     Falls\nF. Falls     Falls     No change     No change\nG. Falls     Falls     Falls     No change\nH. No change     Falls     Falls     No change\nI. Falls     No change     Falls     Falls\nJ. No change     No change     No change     Falls\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0240.wav", "input_sha256": "154117989fadd90d956e10dfbc8d3854bbaa117798f7b58f7dd5bfd88c51546e", "input_samples": 682200, "input_s": 42.638, "n_real_chunks": 43, "score": 0.5099, "act": 0.9992, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "The correct answer is E. Short- run GDP falls, short-run price level falls, long-run GDP falls, and long-run price level falls.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 42, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 10, "fe