{"id": "q0254", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3537916282, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "1bd884090589f25ac8e99f9bb754f4b90b4c7a09d6887616d0aefbdba25a74d4", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 7, "query": "You bought a limousine for $98,000 and are planning to rent it for weddings, ceremonies and parties at $245 per hour. If you estimate the car will be hired for 2 hours a day on average, with daily costs at about $50, what is the estimated yearly yield on your investment if you work all year round, i.e. every day of the year, including any festivities and weekends?\n\nA. 150%\nB. 0.45%\nC. 0.164%\nD. 1.64%\nE. 183%\nF. 2.45%\nG. 245%\nH. 164%\nI. 75%\nJ. 200%\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0254.wav", "input_sha256": "b1a9e32a7e1cee67166e18580ae4c6a2b97ee83203eecad24be0756791da3407", "input_samples": 606000, "input_s": 37.875, "n_real_chunks": 38, "score": 0.7686, "act": 0.9996, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "The correct answer is G, 1 6 4%. Here's why. First, calculate the daily revenue: $2 4 5 per hour times 2 hours equals $ 49 0 per day. Next, subtract the daily costs of $ 50, resulting in a net daily profit of $4 40. Over a year with 3 65 days, this amounts to about $1 6 0,4 00. To find the yield, divide the annual profit by the initial cost of $9 8,00 0 and multiply by 10 0 to get a percentage, which gives approximately 1 6 4%. So, the estimated yearly yield on your investment is around 1 6 4%.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "o